From: Omarchy Shield contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tegra: reset Darcy A04 XUSB memory client

The matching recovery driver flushes the XUSB host memory client when
powering down XUSBC, and normally releases it during power-up. Describe
that reset in the A04 XUSBC power domain so the existing PMC reset-array
sequence also blocks/drains and releases the MC client around startup.
Retain the original CAR reset, using the MC-then-CAR order already used
by the VI domain. No new register-writing implementation is needed.

A bounded A04 RAM test after normal recovery host-driver removal failed
the firmware DMA load with the original reset list. Adding only this
MC reset restored firmware loading, both root hubs, SuperSpeed SanDisk
enumeration and the exact owned-partition read-only admission check.
Full storage/desktop acceptance is a separate qualification.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210-p2894-0050-a04.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210-p2894-0050-a04.dts
@@ -76,3 +76,9 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/* Release an inherited host MC flush when powering XUSBC back up. */
+&pd_xusbhost {
+	resets = <&mc TEGRA210_MC_RESET_XUSB_HOST>,
+		 <&tegra_car TEGRA210_CLK_XUSB_HOST>;
+};
